This project presents a dynamic Power BI dashboard built to analyze and monitor order data. It focuses on key metrics like order volume, revenue, delivery trends, and customer satisfaction—supporting smarter decisions in e-commerce, logistics, or operations teams.

🧠 Objective

To design an interactive, insightful dashboard that helps stakeholders:
Track orders and revenue over time
Identify high-performing products or regions
Understand customer behavior and satisfaction trends
Detect bottlenecks in order processing or delivery

📊 Key Metrics

Total Orders
Total Revenue
Average Order Value
Orders by Region / Product / Category
On-Time Delivery Rate

🧹 Data Cleaning & Modeling

Cleaned raw data using Power Query (null handling, renaming, type conversion)
Built a star schema model with fact and dimension tables (Orders, Customers, Products, Regions, etc.)
Created calculated columns and DAX measures for metrics like AOV and delivery performance

📈 Visuals Included

KPI Cards for quick insights
Line/Area charts for order and revenue trends
Bar charts for product and region comparisons
Donut/Pie charts for category breakdowns
Tables for detailed order-level drilldowns
Slicers for Date, Region, Category, and more

🛠 Tools Used

Power BI Desktop
Power Query
DAX

📂 How to Use

Open Order Dashboard.pbix in Power BI Desktop
Refresh data if source is connected
Interact with slicers to explore different views
Extend with new visuals, measures, or data sources as needed


